' 7. Take speaking test
' Use case: Take speaking test (Practice) · Actor: Learner · Secondary: Azure Speech, AI service (Anthropic Claude)
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Adapter: «interface» PronunciationAssessor → AzurePronunciationAssessor, «interface» SpeakingContentGrader →
'     ClaudeContentGrader wrap the outside services (services/speaking/)
'   - Dependency injection: createSpeakingTestService({ assessor, grader }) receives them (null when not configured;
'     tests inject fakes)
'   - Unit of work: the attempt and the streak day are saved in one transaction
'   - Repository
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens and outside services, «control» use-case logic (controllers,
' services, and the adapter interfaces in front of outside services), «entity» stored data (repository, stores);
' the database keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 07 Take speaking test
title 7. Take speaking test
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Learner
boundary "Web app" as Web
control "Speaking controller" as Ctrl
control "Speaking test\nservice" as Svc
control "«interface»\nPronunciationAssessor" as Assessor
control "«interface»\nSpeakingContentGrader" as Grader
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB
boundary "Azure Speech" as Azure
boundary "AI service\n(Claude)" as AI

note over Svc, Grader : «Dependency injection»: createSpeakingTestService({ assessor, grader })

Learner -> Web : pick a task (N3+), record the answer
Web -> Ctrl : POST /api/speaking-tests/tasks/:taskId/attempts (recording)
Ctrl -> Svc : submitAnswer()
Svc -> Repo : level reached? daily limit left?
alt not reached / limit used
  Svc --> Web : 403 / 429
end
opt Azure Speech configured
  Svc -> Assessor : assess(recording, reference)
  note right of Assessor : «Adapter»\nAzurePronunciationAssessor
  Assessor -> Azure : pronunciation assessment
  Azure --> Assessor : transcript, word scores, fluency
  Assessor --> Svc : our own result type
end
opt AI grading configured
  Svc -> Grader : grade(task, transcript)
  note right of Grader : «Adapter»\nClaudeContentGrader
  Grader -> AI : grading prompt
  AI --> Grader : content score, corrections, feedback
  Grader --> Svc : our own result type
end
alt nothing heard / off task
  Svc --> Web : "no answer" (nothing saved)
end
Svc -> Svc : combine criteria → score and band (JF Standard)
group «Unit of work» withTransaction()
  Svc -> Repo : save attempt (transcript + scores, **never the recording**)
  Svc -> Repo : record streak day
  Repo -> DB : INSERT speaking_attempts …
end
Svc -> Svc : reward "speaking_test" (XP)
Ctrl --> Web : result
Web --> Learner : score, band, feedback, "+XP"
@enduml
